      "evidence": "The definition calls both F2 and the single map F0: 1'→F(1) “natural transformations,” then says that F0 is a “natural isomorphism.” Its cited dependency def-natural-isomorphism defines one as a natural transformation alpha:F⇒G, i.e. a family of components indexed by a source category. F0 is one morphism between two objects, not such a family; it should be required to be an isomorphism, not a natural isomorphism.",
