      "evidence": "Step 1.1 says “* has the same unit because” lambda(1⊗1)lambda^-1=1. This proves only 1*1=1, not 1*f=f=f*1 for arbitrary f. The cited thm-eckmann-hilton-argument requires two unital operations with the same unit, and def-semigroup-and-monoid defines a unit as two-sided for every element. Thus the hypothesis of [L3] has not been established when step 3.1 invokes it. Naturality of both unitors plus their equality on the tensor unit could repair the gap, but neither calculation is supplied here.",
